{"id": "EUVD-2026-86108", "enisaUuid": "0fac1a19-0e47-3782-ba7c-9f5742284d29", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nthunderbolt: Release request if tb_cfg_request() fails in __tb_xdomain_response()\n\nIf tb_cfg_request() fails setting up the request (for example the\ncontrol channel is shut down already) it returns an error without\ncalling the callback. To avoid leaking that memory, call\ntb_cfg_request_put() if tb_cfg_request() fails.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:05:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:59:08", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dbc8a8dd7c1930043c473818fcadcf88cb5e1c4d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/487ee7dbad21d1e757f5dd490ac182aebfa5f689", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/000189b249e45e63ee873d0c59c3be1805349681", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d6657674919bef57c8a7195170263f3456e9876", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/42dddadf6b6131af4d12bfa8bdc84ef954e8cef8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0325d017bf4354a015a02413ee1c7e51266cecf4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4c63f29872cb444b33665348bbd2f45cab06afcd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97510", "GHSA-rcq8-h22x-4p97"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0604fccc-ab1f-32c4-85ed-45b22a58cd20", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d1ff70241a275133e1a0258b7c23588b122276c8 <487ee7dbad21d1e757f5dd490ac182aebfa5f689"}, {"id": "0f3622e9-5f97-38c0-844e-bab9f233f876", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "13127151-d2a5-3680-9366-39cd6deee163", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "1b6d9e45-7bb6-36b7-88b6-4c656ebcb858", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "1dc43638-fd61-3d13-9381-a69f95005fc2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "produc